    {
      "id": "a09eefa89dae7c8adc96b9f5615ff8bebc81512c",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2685909937,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I believe the behavior of invalid characters of dissector preferences would be to assert and prevent Wireshark from really running, so the preference can be fixed.  Why wouldn't we want that with extcap too?",
          "author": {
            "id": 8399509,
            "username": "mmann78",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Michael Mann",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fad119898ba16a3f8be2f765dcff399098444abd4f85a04d4c3ef415a2bbe3d9?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/mmann78"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-08-13T14:51:54.845Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-08-13T14:51:54.845Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 407004095,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20873,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "917ddd31f85d706da837dac6bd62dce193828fd9",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2686061477,
          "type": null,
          "body": "My main issue is with the Table extcap widget where the user can provide their own option names. I want them to be able to provide a GUID (that has a dash for instance) and extcap to handle preferences for this option. If the name is a GUID, it's an invalid preference name, but we want options to be stored anyways. Currently we're stripping the dashes (-), but if the user adds a space, or some other characters that could be of use in another use case, wireshark crashes on an assert.",
          "author": {
            "id": 26787327,
            "username": "gpotter2",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gabriel",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/26787327/avatar.png?v=1788683325",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/gpotter2"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-08-13T15:54:54.373Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-08-13T15:56:30.703Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 407004095,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20873,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b6aecac69df214bc3184dc498f9b1dd622b0642b",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2686083108,
          "type": null,
          "body": "This maybe wasn't clear but this PR only adds sanitizing to the option names provided by the user (typically when used from the Table widget)",
          "author": {
            "id": 26787327,
            "username": "gpotter2",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gabriel",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/26787327/avatar.png?v=1788683325",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/gpotter2"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-08-13T16:04:18.464Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-08-14T07:01:05.513Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 407004095,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
